{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require cognitive disability safeguards in the Private Parking Code of Practice",
        "additional_details": "People with cognitive and neurological disabilities can face recurring barriers with memory, executive function and individual payment processes. Existing disability duties are broad, but the Private Parking Code of Practice should set out clear practical safeguards for these situations. These should include alternative ways to pay, registration-based arrangements where appropriate, and human review before a minor disability-related mistake becomes a substantial parking charge.",
        "background": "Amend the statutory Private Parking Code of Practice to require reasonable adjustments where cognitive or neurological disabilities affect payment or compliance, including alternative payment arrangements and human review before charges are issued or escalated.",
